// 1-29: the longest rails in the building.
id l1-29
name 1-29 CABLE CAR
tagline the longest rails in the building.
bg city
// RULES: what this room is about, how often each mechanic shows up, how hard each portion is (docs/level-design-rules.md)
main anchor yank pull
mechanics current:19 plank:11 pull:4 anchor:8 yank:5 lift:1 capacitor:4 neon:2 white:3
new -
portion 4.2 hop 2 blocks 2 tall and 2 wide over 3-wide current
portion 5.6 hop 5 one-way planks over current (heights 21331)
portion 6.6 hop 4 pull ports (ceiling, low, low, low), 8-7-8 apart, over current
portion 7.1 capacitor gate 24 tiles away, a block on the way
portion 5.7 drive a rail 10 long, swing a 18 gap (high anchors)
portion 7.8 capacitor gate 26 tiles away, current notch on the way
portion 6.5 capacitor gate 24 tiles away
portion 5 a low ceiling 11 long over a current notch
portion 5 capacitor lift up through gates to the top lane
portion 5.9 hop 6 one-way planks over current (heights 113321)
portion 6.6 drive a rail 12 long, swing a 22 gap (mid, mid anchors)
portion 5.4 drive a rail 8 long, swing a 18 gap (ceiling anchors)
portion 6.3 drive a rail 10 long, swing a 22 gap (ceiling, high anchors)
portion 6.9 neon/white stones nWnWW (2 wide, 4 apart) over current
portion 6.5 drive a rail 8 long, swing a 26 gap (mid, mid anchors)
hardness 6.1
map
